d #edb/ref 17592186554993} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563778} :activity/id #uuid "d79f13d1-043c-58ab-89f2-0282f6144b80" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563764 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563755 :question/id #uuid "eaac4ca3-6936-5237-9e98-3d7aa72b5385"} :step/id #uuid "0b859571-5266-5412-bce5-e8cf5c6397c7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563785}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563778 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402113 :question/id #uuid "3c065292-5916-5335-a2ce-48232ddb8e4c"} :step/id #uuid "3c2b1be3-b138-5354-826d-0d722fe6ba4e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563791}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563785 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311562 :question/id #uuid "32bd0c44-4a18-5100-9555-27f58f065186"} :step/id #uuid "66628ba8-6a25-551d-82f3-4c8835969083" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563803}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563791 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229669 :question/id #uuid "783e954f-0aef-53d9-a6ee-3a8685affb71"} :step/id #uuid "8d6857f9-1674-50e2-bd6e-08e1076f3091" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563764}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563803 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186563702 :question/id #uuid "701145a1-1f00-509b-9c1b-60626233c2a4"} :step/id #uuid "cd08637e-a1a7-546e-8e76-ea7112573f7e"}] :activity/title "Solving Homogeneous Systems of ODEs Using Matrix Methods" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186562936}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186048231 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229142 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228910 :question/id #uuid "26df399d-cd87-5b5d-9f3f-7ced4ca5fd06" :question/math-academy-id "e-21707" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-7x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-7y(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nFind the general solution to the system of ODEs above.\n\n*Hint: ![](images/4c/4c7ca8aa3fb83e7c4ce806080257e8f3b3d5186e19f10649a0bed7202f6501b6.svg) where ![](images/04/0492dd33f8d39d4a74139be25415d6d943888d8ccbf67158690f0960c5334415.svg)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/85/85304407fca2ace2d7fb5d97123e1f27f45386c8f3ebcc1a1c3859d1b573d2b0.svg)\nwhere ![](images/81/81bcc770826e2156f310569f014356cc686541259c11aa190ac28394a6d38725.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/31/310669815cad029379ffa4022fa9094ef8597d91496c57f70c66ed51926836b3.svg)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix $\\Phi_0(t)$ of the system is given by\n![](images/e1/e128d7d4610a3a9021b1391f278822bcdf113570500b822c05370e473923f5b7.svg)\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-7t} & t{e}^{-7t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{-7t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{-7t} \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}t{e}^{-7t} \\\\ {e}^{-7t}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-7t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}t \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-7t},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $c_1,c_2 \\in \\mathbb{R}.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5bc609b-dc5b-52e9-9f0e-206f32bb829b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229669 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9e3c6cf5-b1b3-57df-abab-56efb96d89f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (4t) \\\\ \\sin (4t)\\end{bmatrix} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sin (4t) \\\\ \\cos (4t)\\end{bmatrix}e^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228209} {:answer/id #uuid "a0710c2c-0243-5683-af7c-dd5379117712" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (4t) \\\\ \\sin (4t)\\end{bmatrix} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sin (4t) \\\\ \\cos (4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228210} {:answer/id #uuid "e8fa826d-432e-567c-b648-b350c15d4141" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (4t) \\\\ \\sin (4t)\\end{bmatrix}e^{4t} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sin (4t) \\\\ \\cos (4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228211} {:answer/id #uuid "02570066-a4ba-5ed7-9532-5cfdb98488c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (4t) \\\\ \\sin (4t)\\end{bmatrix} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sin (4t) \\\\ \\cos (4t)\\end{bmatrix}e^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228212} {:answer/id #uuid "310ab06b-a4b2-54bf-bfab-dcc138d0d2d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t) = c_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\cos (4t) \\\\ \\sin (4t)\\end{bmatrix} + c_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\sin (4t) \\\\ \\cos (4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228213}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6e4f9160-e954-5fed-b512-345d3c9abd75" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228208} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3be54f80-3e00-5c60-8d2c-859b73f1b04a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402121} {:answer/id #uuid "a489112a-2e25-5139-8701-0da71be4eaed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402122} {:answer/id #uuid "f40839a9-1ee4-555c-b0e0-836cd8ef8a5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402123} {:answer/id #uuid "d13024ed-e948-5192-b456-f8fc65a79957" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{4t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402124} {:answer/id #uuid "2d239718-30d6-534b-aa0f-8cec27c7ffe8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402125}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402125} :answer-field/id #uuid "bbee732a-a84c-5f81-aebe-d7513334919d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402120}] :question/id #uuid "783e954f-0aef-53d9-a6ee-3a8685affb71" :question/math-academy-id "q-334772" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=-4y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=4x(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -4 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) & -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(4t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(4t)\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229677 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5392cdab-374c-5ae2-97a2-f4228e352881" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305962} {:answer/id #uuid "7a6f36b6-4121-5cab-9216-833c7c62083f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186306320} {:answer/id #uuid "d1e11b73-c7d1-59c9-abf2-19d051435206" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-3t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307100} {:answer/id #uuid "f3ca31cf-3864-5198-b515-c7ff18c474da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307408} {:answer/id #uuid "f507092b-2755-5654-9fcc-edf25726ea51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307419}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186307408} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0ef5c61-1dd5-5887-92a7-99cd1e43fe22" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308031}] :question/id #uuid "56cd9daa-00e7-5df3-81ab-61efadc99e76" :question/math-academy-id "q-335023" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following gives the general solution to the system of ODEs above?\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,c \\\\  & ={e}^{At}\\,c \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{c}_{1} \\\\ {c}_{2}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(3t) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(3t)\\end{bmatrix},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${c}_{1},{c}_{2}\\in R.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186308684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "488cb1f7-d8f3-5937-97b2-5b2c3a66bfcd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x(t)={c}_{1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{6t}+{c}_{2}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}{e}^{-6t}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186305859} {:answer/id #uuid "7cea238c-07f8-5863-ba42-90a0781222f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :an