lution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311562 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2dcee7af-7056-5b97-9372-e26001db1e4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309094} {:answer/id #uuid "54b88482-9a48-53c8-b436-71c2a5fcea44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4t{e}^{6t} \\\\ -4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309389} {:answer/id #uuid "6b578480-7196-5ccc-b193-d86e5994a039" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}4t{e}^{6t} \\\\ -4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309581} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a02da3-4c0e-59a8-9ef3-fc732675a0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4t{e}^{-6t} \\\\ -4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310315} {:answer/id #uuid "c60df48c-c6c5-573d-a4c8-6c244c51b408" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4{e}^{6t} \\\\ -4t{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310339}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4t{e}^{6t} \\\\ -4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309389} :answer-field/id #uuid "84cab197-81f5-503d-a0d6-83d5086f95b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311161}] :question/id #uuid "32bd0c44-4a18-5100-9555-27f58f065186" :question/math-academy-id "q-335268" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=6x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=6y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{6t} & t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{6t} & t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{6t} & t{e}^{6t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4t{e}^{6t} \\\\ -4{e}^{6t}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311563 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ec0f445-fd55-5daa-b03e-51ba5822b429" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3t{e}^{5t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-5t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308851} {:answer/id #uuid "36a44ee2-66ef-5d90-afc8-0c7af60b9e7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3t{e}^{-5t} \\\\ -3{e}^{-5t}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309164} {:answer/id #uuid "452bb80d-4b01-50cd-95bb-65ff7db4cdee" :answer/type {:db/ident :