& \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 9 \\\\ 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(9t) \\\\ 4\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(9t)\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186555774 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c48896b-a018-521e-946b-fe65b686effd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -5\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555247} {:answer/id #uuid "7a745ab5-2e30-5358-a661-1005ce9fee4d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555285} {:answer/id #uuid "8e5a344b-c228-5070-a3de-d96f53cbd405" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555331} {:answer/id #uuid "cf972ef6-5de2-58b9-b5d8-6de313e595af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555494} {:answer/id #uuid "da11d876-2fe9-5885-b371-78fffbd4906e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555331} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9bfc61d-9208-5f2a-9171-0d8c90db3cd8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186555756}] :question/id #uuid "27a5f814-886e-5a61-acf9-facf209e99cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-335263" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(0) \\\\ y(0)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the solution of the initial value problem can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)\\,x(0),\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system, and $x(0)$ is the initial condition vector.\n\nNow, using the given information, the standard fundamental matrix ${Φ}_{0}(t)$ of the system is given by\n\n$$\n{Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,x(0) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving a Homogeneous Initial Value Problem Using a Given Matrix Exponential"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229144 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186228917 :question/id #uuid "b061f2b1-b015-582f-921f-9b444db631ee" :question/math-academy-id "e-21723" :question/problem "![](images/b0/b0d7ecb854b93b475f1897f7ae66e0e459a5ad22247a9d9a5c11adff32b747e4.svg)\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ![](images/50/50c3d207258cc321a19532b7b54da568a4a6361dde55f35247fe60e931fe5f93.svg) where ![](images/59/599d579a41d84635ae3a34867759b69af6b406d433c4c11a53898f69e856371e.svg)*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n![](images/6d/6dfab7c1edb51450a9238b3fd1154c7d4a5dccb47c689c54768c4b6cc952c068.svg)\nwhere ![](images/eb/eb99201c10627a06594c4967ac8f3a56cb75784f1f824332a9b58a10aaf672bc.svg) So, the matrix of the system is ![](images/e7/e70ec908edd1985f4f1f719dceee192536c0bcdf0b4deedcf1c9f785005ee041.svg)\n\nGiven the system $\\mathbf{x}'(t) = A \\mathbf{x}(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi(t) \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $\\mathbf{c}$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t) = \\Phi_0(t) \\mathbf{c} =e^{At} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nwhere $\\Phi_0(t) = e^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t = t_0,$ we have \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x}(t_0) = e^{At_0} \\, \\mathbf{c},\n$$\n\nand since $e^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{c} = e^{-At_0} \\, \\mathbf{x}(t_0).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $\\mathbf{x}(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(7(t-1)) \\\\ 3\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(7(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "37e58bb6-6d90-5171-bba2-6ffa5a0c91d9" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229664 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5bfd4a6b-0cff-5025-ac15-1ba07589a334" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541606}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "e^{2(t-1)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541606} :answer-field/id #uuid "c00aedbd-3d32-591a-9238-e662e5a71296" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228182} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "36d6d80b-bee2-5ffe-978c-9a216b9c3522" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541538}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186541538} :answer-field/id #uuid "7397605e-8fc4-5376-8bac-4c5dbc127439" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228183}] :question/id #uuid "77f295d1-1cbb-5b17-a7ef-414238a16c0a" :question/math-academy-id "q-334547" :question/problem "$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t)=2x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t)=2y(t),\\end{aligned}\\,[\\begin{aligned}x(1) \\\\ y(1)\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2t} & t{e}^{2t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2t}\\end{aligned}],$ where $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}]=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"80px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{aligned}].$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-1)}\\,x(1) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(t-1)} & (t-1){e}^{2(t-1)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{2(t-1)}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\,{e}^{2(t-1)}\\, \\\\ \\,0\\,\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186229684 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "59d8cb4f-ee06-5141-9f71-0005f275d41d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481984} {:answer/id #uuid "65ee1f50-cf6b-58b8-afd8-663783704016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482010} {:answer/id #uuid "7e285e86-01d4-53c2-bae8-84c094816e4b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482063} {:answer/id #uuid "d4207d80-a6eb-5165-8ab9-aace8ee2daa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482281} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c4b7e3-8500-59d1-966d-52216ee1c994" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482291}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482291} :answer-field/id #uuid "283ab639-7505-5578-b135-707cc7103815" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186228298}] :question/id #uuid "8b9edfd9-1c2b-58af-aab6-8f8f25829073" :question/math-academy-id "q-335447" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=6y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=6x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(3) \\\\ y(3)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 6 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-3)}\\,x(3) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(6(t-3)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(6(t-3))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311564 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01f8dc2a-d1c1-50ad-9080-e4aea1133091" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3(t-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308761}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{3(t-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308761} :answer-field/id #uuid "93eace97-bb5c-5bd2-b8df-7eca81320545" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311212} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07bdd633-a0bf-5ddf-ac96-58b9d4b0f277" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(t-2){e}^{3(t-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308806}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(t-2){e}^{3(t-2)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308806} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6cac817-7eaa-5d9c-919e-8afb3c166bfa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311466}] :question/id #uuid "80bead61-fb6c-5bf6-88d2-511e52d01763" :question/math-academy-id "q-335273" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=3x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=3y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(2) \\\\ y(2)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3t} & t{e}^{3t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n| $\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-2)}\\,x(2) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{3(t-2)} & (t-2){e}^{3(t-2)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{3(t-2)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\,(t-2){e}^{3(t-2)}\\, \\\\ \\,{e}^{3(t-2)}\\,\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311590 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ac977920-e0a4-5694-ad1f-49081b7d03d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-{e}^{t-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310141} {:answer/id #uuid "0344a228-63e9-598d-8026-7a699136dec3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^{t-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445537}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-e^{t-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445537} :answer-field/id #uuid "447e90ea-b52f-52cf-bb01-3ef584ba8bc3" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310977} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5260c675-dc05-52d0-9bae-47c544593fa6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5-t){e}^{t-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309370} {:answer/id #uuid "9de2ee31-7f56-539c-b879-55f626705e5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5-t)e^{t-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5-t)e^{t-4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445578} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2f58c80-ac07-53a4-8d29-caca1289055a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311498}] :question/id #uuid "7467b4a4-4b5f-508d-a258-892c78866514" :question/math-academy-id "q-335429" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(4) \\\\ y(4)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t} & t{e}^{t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"100px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-4)}\\,x(4) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{t-4} & (t-4){e}^{t-4} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{t-4}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\,(5-t){e}^{t-4}\\, \\\\ \\,-{e}^{t-4}\\,\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311591 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d91f4d02-d2a8-5b28-bafa-cf715ccd725b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2t-6){e}^{7(t+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310495} {:answer/id #uuid "7e39c819-e178-5bfa-a5fb-cd7dfa304efa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2(t+3)e^{7(t+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445567}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2(t+3)e^{7(t+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445567} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ad223ca-9907-5787-a8f2-d130b39c34e4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311031} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c9f1f2f-a7f9-5f8e-b0f6-b5b812c958b8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2{e}^{7(t+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309857} {:answer/id #uuid "c4391037-0726-5baa-bba4-61f44fdba73c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2e^{7(t+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445583}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-2e^{7(t+3)}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445583} :answer-field/id #uuid "81289e93-97cd-57a8-8c4b-99b0e66ee827" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311149}] :question/id #uuid "467988d5-2a79-550a-9715-201ca6f86285" :question/math-academy-id "q-335430" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=7x(t)+y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=7y(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(-3) \\\\ y(-3)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{7t} & t{e}^{7t} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{7t}\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"140px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t+3)}\\,x(-3) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}{e}^{7(t+3)} & (t+3){e}^{7(t+3)} \\\\ 0 & {e}^{7(t+3)}\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\,(-2t-6){e}^{7(t+3)}\\, \\\\ \\,-2{e}^{7(t+3)}\\,\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311592 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6a22e898-470d-5e85-9a6c-1224cd8777f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{cos}(8(t+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309570} {:answer/id #uuid "f947e9b5-78ea-57fb-a267-4b7bbb84d360" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos(8(t+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445592}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\cos(8(t+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445592} :answer-field/id #uuid "3b0e62b0-582b-5d3a-9477-33f4077f2b98" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310951} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f8550c3-f522-5258-8e0b-73324de5b1ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\operatorname{sin}(8(t+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310036} {:answer/id #uuid "81738d4b-ad6c-5c58-9652-7aa7295f8d23" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sin(8(t+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445570}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sin(8(t+1))" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186445570} :answer-field/id #uuid "e95a834d-03cb-586d-9850-7d2b0447898e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311474}] :question/id #uuid "b7870a76-0c90-529a-9ddb-a95d0acab0af" :question/math-academy-id "q-335437" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=8y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=-8x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(-1) \\\\ y(-1)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8t) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*\n\n<table align=\"l\" cellpadding=\"0\" rules=\"all\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"30px\" rowspan=\"2\">$\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}=\\,\\,$</td>\n<td align=\"center\" height=\"40px\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"120px\">{{field-1}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\" width=\"5px\"></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n<td align=\"center\">{{field-2}}</td>\n<td align=\"center\"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table>" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 8 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t+1)}\\,x(-1) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1)) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1)) & \\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\,5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8(t+1))\\, \\\\ \\,5\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8(t+1))\\,\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311593 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05145451-fcbb-5f80-80f4-d64ca99158d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186308785} {:answer/id #uuid "2688d629-3656-5e97-b595-427198fca4e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309035} {:answer/id #uuid "3a754278-1ce8-526e-8394-488305b11d44" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309196} {:answer/id #uuid "3ba34ae1-921c-54e5-95ff-dddb6c8b72f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309208} {:answer/id #uuid "b3059e56-805a-5121-8205-eed50f4c7547" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310195}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310195} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c203e1b-e42c-5a3a-a497-dcca694fd0f3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311131}] :question/id #uuid "55bee6bc-3983-5e41-8e4f-3cb5fd416427" :question/math-academy-id "q-335449" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=5y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=5x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(2) \\\\ y(2)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have\n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-2)}\\,x(2) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(5(t-2)) \\\\ -\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(5(t-2))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186311594 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86261b72-d394-5cfd-a0a0-49b007d2681d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186309795} {:answer/id #uuid "b856e9b8-a6be-5887-8145-46f0e749762f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310239} {:answer/id #uuid "bcb07f3a-e3ba-518d-bbd5-493ab6cd327a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310277} {:answer/id #uuid "dce11e6d-2948-5678-bbb4-3c9a68ec1cfb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310518} {:answer/id #uuid "eba6cc7e-d63d-5b40-a9c3-dc0d6d53a2c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186310623} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3933d4d-0b43-5fcd-a810-0bb81c6bd727" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311452}] :question/id #uuid "9289fbe7-7bd9-5d14-8bb7-6c1df9b50bb4" :question/math-academy-id "q-335451" :question/problem "$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}^{′}(t) &=2y(t) \\\\ {y}^{′}(t) &=2x(t),\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\begin{bmatrix}x(-2) \\\\ y(-2)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nFind the solution to the initial value problem above.\n\n*Hint: ${e}^{At}=\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2t) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2t)\\end{bmatrix},$ where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$*" :question/worked-solution "Writing our system in matrix form, we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{′}(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}x(t),\n$$\n\nwhere $x(t)=\\begin{bmatrix}x(t) \\\\ y(t)\\end{bmatrix}.$ So, the matrix of the system is $A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$\n\nGiven the system ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t),$ where $A$ is a constant square matrix, the general solution of the system can be written as\n\n$$\nx(t)=Φ(t)\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere $Φ(t)$ is a fundamental matrix of the system, and $c$ is a constant vector.\n\nSo, we can write our general solution as\n\n$$\nx(t)={Φ}_{0}(t)c={e}^{At}\\,c,\n$$\n\nwhere ${Φ}_{0}(t)={e}^{At}$ is the standard fundamental matrix of the system. Substituting $t={t}_{0},$ we have \n\n$$\nx({t}_{0})={e}^{A{t}_{0}}\\,c,\n$$\n\nand since ${e}^{At}$ is invertible for all $t,$ we have\n\n$$\nc={e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}).\n$$\n\nPlugging the above back into our expression for $x(t),$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{At}\\,{e}^{-A{t}_{0}}\\,x({t}_{0}) \\\\  & ={e}^{A(t-{t}_{0})}\\,x({t}_{0}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x(t) & ={e}^{A(t-(-2))}\\,x(-2) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2)) & \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ \\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) & \\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(2(t+2)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(2(t+2))\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186391579 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a3c3294a-f087-5672-a53e-117506420382" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391581} {:answer/id #uuid "601ea9e6-24b0-535e-bb17-49ca178db97e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391582} {:answer/id #uuid "59b758f5-6067-571d-908b-9e50262c9da7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391583} {:answer/id #uuid "66384a82-a5a2-5020-8b9b-8db002bae474" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391584} {:answer/id #uuid "70ed0219-7267-5410-9f26-31afb335cb12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(4(t-1)) \\\\ 2\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(4(t-1))\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186391585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\operatorname{si