 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix},\\,R=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,Y=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "- $S$ is a diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. Also, all the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are zeros.\n\nNotice that $S$ is not an identity matrix since the diagonal entries are not all ones.\n\n- $R$ is *not* a diagonal matrix since it's not a square matrix.\n\n- $Y$ is *not* a diagonal matrix. It's a square matrix since it has the same number of rows and columns. But some of the entries that do not lie on the main diagonal are not zeros (for instance, ${y}_{31}=1\\ne 0$).\n\nTherefore, only $S$ is a diagonal matrix."}] :knowledge-point/title "Identifying a Special Square Matrix"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087698 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087505 :question/id #uuid "0e3ad3cd-f7c4-55f4-8a0b-b850283bc6b0" :question/math-academy-id "e-4393" :question/problem "How can we best describe the following matrix?\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Notice that $F$ is a matrix that has a single column. Therefore, it is a column vector."} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "7b6ddadb-471a-5195-a0f5-fd44bdc8f780" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186510568 :question-generator/id #uuid "59ccd5bd-2e7f-5a1b-9d4e-06ec327ee7f6" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186087698.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088360 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b80d0d6d-a385-5a9f-a38c-76c3157d90c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$E$ and $F$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086814} {:answer/id #uuid "c4407053-838c-5cfe-b16e-a6a789ddf292" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$E$ and $G$ only" :db