swer-field/id #uuid "261b6e2d-0dfe-5831-9e92-dc6f83195792" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265315}] :question/id #uuid "25acca2a-8a8f-54f2-840d-50238b932393" :question/math-academy-id "q-131184" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-4-2\\text{i} & 7+5\\text{i} & 6+6\\text{i} \\\\ -4+5\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 3 \\\\ -2-\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & -3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhat is the value of ${b}_{23}+{b}_{33}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}-4-2\\text{i} & 7+5\\text{i} & 6+6\\text{i} \\\\ -4+5\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & 3 \\\\ -2-\\text{i} & 2-\\text{i} & -3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{-4-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{7+5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{6+6\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-4+5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{3} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-3\\text{i}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4+2\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} & 6-6\\text{i} \\\\ -4-5\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} & 3 \\\\ -2+\\text{i} & 2+\\text{i} & 3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{23}+{b}_{33}=3+3\\text{i}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268912 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "28fac6c8-4931-5bf3-9e3c-2d3cac0ac3ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266506} {:answer/id #uuid "82c8074b-b8e5-5b2b-af0e-b82c872eb5e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267294} {:answer/id #uuid "96b718d1-0474-51c8-a395-fa84ef441b7e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267489} {:answer/id #uuid "aff85835-5338-51c6-85a4-85e132b1fed9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3+\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267728} {:answer/id #uuid "e4732a21-9d73-5a23-8ad9-d776e6f4191f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268162}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266506} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa6d4e59-5d48-587f-8d52-07922757ef65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268712}] :question/id #uuid "0650a246-400c-5ccd-af24-2667ccbb4784" :question/math-academy-id "q-132713" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3-2\\text{i} & 4\\text{i} \\\\ -1-3\\text{i} & 5 & 3-5\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i} & -5-\\text{i} & -3+3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.$ What is the value of ${b}_{31}+{b}_{32}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3-2\\text{i} & 4\\text{i} \\\\ -1-3\\text{i} & 5 & 3-5\\text{i} \\\\ 2+\\text{i} & -5-\\text{i} & -3+3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{-4} & \\overset{―}{3-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-1-3\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{5} & \\overset{―}{3-5\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{2+\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-5-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-3+3\\text{i}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 & 3+2\\text{i} & -4\\text{i} \\\\ -1+3\\text{i} & 5 & 3+5\\text{i} \\\\ 2-\\text{i} & -5+\\text{i} & -3-3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{31}+{b}_{32}=(2-\\text{i})+(-5+\\text{i})=-3.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186268913 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81d6f1ed-851b-545b-aab8-0e739dc2f616" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8-\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267288} {:answer/id #uuid "8f34919e-2f42-5ed3-ad83-b7d74239c918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-4-9\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267422} {:answer/id #uuid "ad12930b-dbe4-5ec9-859a-d1aa529ebd04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267706} {:answer/id #uuid "c047e058-34c8-5ebe-9788-78bec7cd8451" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5-6\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267864} {:answer/id #uuid "cb5c1336-05c6-5615-b4a3-560cc7e3168f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267967}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5-6\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186267864} :answer-field/id #uuid "6aa8f2fa-c66f-5c23-9e93-6de9d0f58952" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186268599}] :question/id #uuid "b1e3099e-fc04-5e9b-8698-7f21fd8d4845" :question/math-academy-id "q-132715" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}3\\text{i} & -2+2\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & -1+5\\text{i} & -3+4\\text{i} \\\\ -5-3\\text{i} & 4-4\\text{i} & 4\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.$ What is the value of ${b}_{12}+{b}_{23}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}3\\text{i} & -2+2\\text{i} & 5-5\\text{i} \\\\ \\text{i} & -1+5\\text{i} & -3+4\\text{i} \\\\ -5-3\\text{i} & 4-4\\text{i} & 4\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{3\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-2+2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{5-5\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-1+5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-3+4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-5-3\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{4-4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{4\\text{i}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3\\text{i} & -2-2\\text{i} & 5+5\\text{i} \\\\ -\\text{i} & -1-5\\text{i} & -3-4\\text{i} \\\\ -5+3\\text{i} & 4+4\\text{i} & -4\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{12}+{b}_{23}=(-2-2\\text{i})+(-3-4\\text{i})=-5-6\\text{i}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345166 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4f8c0abb-ebd3-50ba-aff7-08644e82858f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3-3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342901} {:answer/id #uuid "976288ee-d4b0-5229-92c4-12b825a5393f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343566} {:answer/id #uuid "c91d0de1-b913-5ed7-ab96-6c9cf08e85d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344001} {:answer/id #uuid "e6965016-24de-5fad-84ff-011de2ab5fd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344261} {:answer/id #uuid "f313607b-c44d-524b-9402-3d940c1b734f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3-3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344374}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3+3\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344001} :answer-field/id #uuid "d03bc1fa-0205-5409-af9b-c5c4347e2bf5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344850}] :question/id #uuid "1d571b66-c5ad-536a-9b16-6a2bfe6d32b7" :question/math-academy-id "q-76055" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-2+\\text{i} & 4 & -\\text{i} \\\\ -5\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} & 1 \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i} & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ What is the value of ${b}_{13}+{b}_{31}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}-2+\\text{i} & 4 & -\\text{i} \\\\ -5\\text{i} & 7-5\\text{i} & 1 \\\\ 3-2\\text{i} & \\text{i} & 0\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{-2+\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{4} & \\overset{―}{-\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{7-5\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{1} \\\\ \\overset{―}{3-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{0}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2-\\text{i} & 4 & \\text{i} \\\\ 5\\text{i} & 7+5\\text{i} & 1 \\\\ 3+2\\text{i} & -\\text{i} & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{13}+{b}_{31}=\\text{i}+(3+2\\text{i})=3+3\\text{i}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345168 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "41dd09f6-0939-5506-a351-fbad720a41e7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1+7\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342782} {:answer/id #uuid "624ba52f-cb14-5738-9454-669c81055e83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1-7\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343073} {:answer/id #uuid "63b53a99-7c78-5500-9ec4-14d6307bcd52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7+\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343083} {:answer/id #uuid "72f83b85-6723-5210-94da-dbd63f781e20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7+\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343234} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f74711-7d96-5f76-9b61-e8b9c67d7e37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7-\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343699}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7+\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343083} :answer-field/id #uuid "4dd3289e-d5fa-50f8-884e-179d97dc6e97" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344625}] :question/id #uuid "aad215f0-b1cf-5385-a89c-46aa554c6d26" :question/math-academy-id "q-76057" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}9-7\\text{i} & -2\\text{i} & 6-\\text{i} \\\\ -7 & 5-\\text{i} & \\text{i} \\\\ 6 & -\\text{i} & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$ What is the value of ${b}_{21}+{b}_{32}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}9-7\\text{i} & -2\\text{i} & 6-\\text{i} \\\\ -7 & 5-\\text{i} & \\text{i} \\\\ 6 & -\\text{i} & 0\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{9-7\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-2\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{6-\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-7} & \\overset{―}{5-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{6} & \\overset{―}{-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{0}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9+7\\text{i} & 2\\text{i} & 6+\\text{i} \\\\ -7 & 5+\\text{i} & -\\text{i} \\\\ 6 & \\text{i} & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{21}+{b}_{32}=-7+\\text{i}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345169 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5b59de2f-a0ee-5419-b3d2-cb790998f22f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14-58\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343003} {:answer/id #uuid "6180a17d-b049-58a3-9de0-61dd02cdc373" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1+8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343064} {:answer/id #uuid "807e25d9-1abb-54f6-87b2-f6c414f4a1d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343345} {:answer/id #uuid "9e761fe5-58e1-502b-8641-570195623862" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343635} {:answer/id #uuid "dfcd86c0-0ec0-5ace-b85b-d17927c6ca70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11+5\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344200}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1-8\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343635} :answer-field/id #uuid "92d2eb4b-7b84-5aa0-87ff-12fc495e67b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344746}] :question/id #uuid "49c6019f-3c20-53a6-9816-199ae4484ce7" :question/math-academy-id "q-76059" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}7-\\text{i} & 6+4\\text{i} \\\\ 7-4\\text{i} & 4+9\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.$ What is the value of ${b}_{12}-{b}_{21}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}7-\\text{i} & 6+4\\text{i} \\\\ 7-4\\text{i} & 4+9\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{7-\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{6+4\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{7-4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{4+9\\text{i}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}7+\\text{i} & 6-4\\text{i} \\\\ 7+4\\text{i} & 4-9\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{12}-{b}_{21}=(6-4\\text{i})-(7+4\\text{i})=-1-8\\text{i}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345170 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "42a4a148-20e1-5f80-b2fb-2e042ddedeaa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13-10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342792} {:answer/id #uuid "70ac7ae1-e498-5991-a18f-f32e7ba35ab1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3-4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343205} {:answer/id #uuid "9e230392-c27c-5f5e-afcd-0b32e220638b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3+10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343630} {:answer/id #uuid "ab258033-56cd-5b22-a1bb-024fda97b989" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3+4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343744} {:answer/id #uuid "eb08a5f6-2f5c-5f17-92cf-20683e6d82ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13-4\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344294}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-13-10\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342792} :answer-field/id #uuid "781fb444-d63a-5572-8368-68f65b8913c4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344711}] :question/id #uuid "3500d72d-18ba-52aa-afec-29c407f01547" :question/math-academy-id "q-76061" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}5+4\\text{i} & -6\\text{i} \\\\ -5+7\\text{i} & 8-3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.$ What is the value of ${b}_{21}-{b}_{22}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}5+4\\text{i} & -6\\text{i} \\\\ -5+7\\text{i} & 8-3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{5+4\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{-6\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{-5+7\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{8-3\\text{i}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5-4\\text{i} & 6\\text{i} \\\\ -5-7\\text{i} & 8+3\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{21}-{b}_{22}=(-5-7\\text{i})-(8+3\\text{i})=-13-10\\text{i}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345171 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0145ff6a-5280-53e6-a6f5-4aaa362caf43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11-2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342259} {:answer/id #uuid "36ceabd8-3d58-54a8-8e9e-45477e8187f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11+12\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342689} {:answer/id #uuid "75f5c19f-ae62-5e2d-ac7d-c938849911c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7+12\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343255} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d049ed-e856-596c-8f9d-6bbcfc6ed7be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7+2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186343736} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe51bb1-4a25-578f-b0b5-2664e189773f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-7-2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "11-2\\text{i}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186342259} :answer-field/id #uuid "37d25c56-f9b9-5817-a980-760c25858499" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186344588}] :question/id #uuid "b7c1df80-7eb0-5daa-99fe-321f16fa32cd" :question/math-academy-id "q-76063" :question/problem "Find $B=\\overset{―}{A}$, where $A=\\begin{bmatrix}-3+6\\text{i} & 2+7\\text{i} \\\\ 9 & 9-5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.$ What is the value of ${b}_{12}+{b}_{22}?$" :question/worked-solution "Taking the complex conjugate of each entry, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{―}{A} & =\\overset{―}{\\begin{bmatrix}-3+6\\text{i} & 2+7\\text{i} \\\\ 9 & 9-5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\overset{―}{-3+6\\text{i}} & \\overset{―}{2+7\\text{i}} \\\\ \\overset{―}{9} & \\overset{―}{9-5\\text{i}}\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3-6\\text{i} & 2-7\\text{i} \\\\ 9 & 9+5\\text{i}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${b}_{12}+{b}_{22}=(2-7\\text{i})+(9+5\\text{i})=11-2\\text{i}.$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Complex Conjugate of a Complex Matrix"}] :topic/math-academy-id 2015 :topic/title "Matrices Over the Complex Numbers"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134695} :activity/id #uuid "93a7b58c-f55f-5517-ad99-318bb8790e55" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134695 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135059 :tutorial/content "Let's consider the following system of linear equations:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=-2 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=4 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nIt is easy to show that the system is inconsistent (i.e., it has no solution). However, in real-world problems, we might want to find an approximate solution to the system. \n\nLet's formulate the problem a little more rigorously. Firstly, we write down the system in the form $A\\mathbf x = \\mathbf b\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/22/22b8abd4638e579875755f482442cf1dbf89653bd9d396b4a802217e25177839.svg)\n\nWe are interested in vectors $\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}$ such that $A\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}$ is very close to $\\mathbf b.$ More precisely, we wish to *minimize the distance* between $A\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}$ and $\\mathbf b.$ Recall that the distance between $A\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}$ and $\\mathbf b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\Vert  A{\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}} - \\mathbf{b} \\Vert.\n$$\n\nThe smaller the value of $\\Vert  A{\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}} - \\mathbf{b} \\Vert,$ the better our approximation $\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}$ will be. \n\nIn terms of vector subspaces, we wish to find a vector $A{\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}$ that lies in $\\textrm{Col}(A)$ and is closest to $\\mathbf{b}.$\nTherefore, $A{\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}$ must be the orthogonal projection of $\\mathbf{b}$ onto the subspace spanned by the columns of $A.$\n\n![](images/3a/3a1c79036954f0e04212892b7e3d79c75f8cd7b81d7785441f090f89a4eb6faf.png)\n\nIt can be shown that ${\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}$ is found by solving the corresponding **normal equation**, given by \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe'll prove this at the end of the lesson. Note that the normal equation is obtained by left-multiplying the equation $A {\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}} = \\mathbf b$ by $A^T.$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix $A^T \\! A$ is invertible. Therefore, left-multiplying the normal equation by $(A^T \\! A)^{-1},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}} = (A^T \\! A)^{-1}A^T \\mathbf{b}.\n$$\n\nWe now compute the right-hand side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -4 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -4 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 18\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{99}\\begin{bmatrix}18 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -20\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{8}{33} \\\\ -\\frac{38}{33}\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vector ${\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}$ is called the **least-squares solution** of the given system.\n\n**Watch out!** We assumed that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, which guarantees that $A^T \\! A\\,$ is invertible. However, if the columns of $A$ are linearly *dependent,* then we have to use a different approach to solve the problem." :tutorial/id #uuid "548ecdec-2401-51e1-b2cf-d63f0b5a595d" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3636 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "c3719452-213a-5a8f-92fa-ac5912c1a8ba" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134697}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134696 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133799 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74efec6b-6e5f-5761-a116-5c94e3fb4326"} :step/id #uuid "eb5011df-f314-5469-89c6-7bc2e1633d5b" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134778}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134697 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133800 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "d23c4292-6fdd-5cba-a2e7-0f4d770b2309"} :step/id #uuid "bd48fc68-e028-5256-934f-98b803b1f3f4" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134696}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134778 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133848 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5924037a-ddc3-5f50-b4b0-1bd813cef255"} :step/id #uuid "e9d074bb-35df-566a-80ad-6c15d1e9fe5f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134892}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134892 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135146 :tutorial/content "Suppose that ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) is an ![](images/67/677276828b5438bcf8d73facec02bc738e2e4f02bb6c5ff83bd5ae41902dd8ea.svg) matrix with linearly independent columns. We'll now explain why the least-squares solution ![](images/a4/a4d10ece37c4369a97f57734306d77d35e94a240b68f2625b4d45791bdc13378.svg) to the least-squares problem \n\n![](images/f7/f72b4cb4f9fd00c6a409ed62ae97aad9915179065d14609810459cbd7b5b63c2.svg)\n\ncan be found by solving the normal equation\n![](images/dc/dcd7a5cf3452038ee326ed1b4a5ab2913f41ad408849ddda132cbdfee7c35887.svg)\n\nThe vector ![](images/eb/eba4e0fbcf4207b493c3a3a4eecc12df848d9d995708881cce8542ae5d04bdd9.svg) must be the orthogonal projection of ![](images/63/639196a1a30d6f6280e3cf491e6cf3c2b0b991892970f7b641a9b300defb034f.svg) onto the subspace spanned by the columns of ![](images/c8/c8c72090d28b539bed2177052b06540383d63ac720008f1b301dafcac4fa6227.svg)\n\n![](images/02/024c12b780df0414ab1cf012e5733603fb1167c9533e199c46628d73ad12ebd9.png)\n\nAs a result, we have that\n\n![](images/c3/c3f058a925aef4913b39914985d02cfb3d7b2752c0116aa43b2e73d804fa29d4.svg) \n\nwhich is equivalent to saying that ![](images/c5/c54ecdc03925384b80bdbddc9df105fb34d4b31426570aa7c6446815c6a90ed9.svg) is orthogonal to each column ![](images/16/162e4a7398d3a8c47cc967b78bf43167256270c609bfdc271e46a2ea32ade145.svg) of ![](images/c8/c8c72090d28b539bed2177052b06540383d63ac720008f1b301dafcac4fa6227.svg) Thus, the dot product of the columns of ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) and the vector ![](images/c5/c54ecdc03925384b80bdbddc9df105fb34d4b31426570aa7c6446815c6a90ed9.svg) must be equal to ![](images/37/37dd4bc8064071b5d4219d47ac24847861bdbe0c82b48e4997c5d7d8b4a3d566.svg)\n\n![](images/57/5701e3d1325d0ec137b7d405796114e3044f5076c11fa9e2e10fe70d16919a88.svg)\n\nThis system of equations can be written in terms of matrix products as\n\n![](images/92/921a6627dff46463fc16fc80fe16353fb80942f08c5c632d6665920be96676ed.svg) \n\nFinally, expanding the left-hand side, we obtain our normal equation:\n\n![](images/86/867c103511eeb1e208028ea1a3af3eb4b397c50a3131efea683b55d959d4ec4e.svg)" :tutorial/id #uuid "43d14ff9-b350-5406-9f4b-64096d8f3215" :tutorial/math-academy-id 6154 :tutorial/title "Deriving the Normal Equation"} :step/id #uuid "df64bb85-56ef-5ee5-80d4-956e1d949a18"}] :activity/title "The Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System (Without Collinearity)" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186134026} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500387} :activity/id #uuid "4afc5eb0-b00c-5311-ad64-1f529d40ac87" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500387 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326908 :question/id #uuid "082f22b9-7dbc-5c7c-88d0-775a3d957e87"} :step/id #uuid "0c175108-3251-5f6f-a837-933e8a149a06" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500431}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500391 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500322 :question/id #uuid "7b37b44d-e7cb-5e9e-b8af-e9f1e4941b43"} :step/id #uuid "1daadfd6-2782-5d18-911b-b764bf042f15"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500431 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354410 :question/id #uuid "22b88813-fc85-5da7-b050-31934e04cdb3"} :step/id #uuid "a561b4d8-a24f-5ea9-9176-71cdc5599a2d" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500445}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500445 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186354439 :question/id #uuid "48fc2839-660f-57b5-b91c-b2fcd5bae103"} :step/id #uuid "d22a3088-3980-554b-950c-e1334497ac66" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500452}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500452 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382559 :question/id #uuid "cbf886ad-eced-5102-99df-0e48cd09970a"} :step/id #uuid "efc7b297-2494-521d-8ca9-fb8275cf05d1" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500391}}] :activity/title "The Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System (Without Collinearity)" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499645}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186048284 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133799 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186133608 :question/id #uuid "e7fb27f0-67b3-58fa-a582-acd4a4ebe045" :question/math-academy-id "e-5588" :question/problem "Find the least-squares solution to the system of linear equations given below. You're given that the columns of the corresponding coefficient matrix are linearly independent.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}-2{x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=12 \\\\ {x}_{1}-2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=0 \\\\ -{x}_{2}-2{x}_{3} &=-12 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{3} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $A \\mathbf{x} = \\mathbf{b}\\mathbin{:}$\n![](images/cf/cf50ed91023704d55ddb9874e9c2bd081bce5ab28fb556019d038e55f32c0905.svg)\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution ${\\hat{\\mathbf{x}}}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by $A^T\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix $A^T \\! A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $(A^T \\! A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -12 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-24 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-24 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 24\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "74efec6b-6e5f-5761-a116-5c94e3fb4326" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134363 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b22d729-cc0d-54fa-9864-c8d4080046cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324200} {:answer/id #uuid "9f17fb7a-58e4-5d4f-958d-026570090fb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325319} {:answer/id #uuid "ec9c2e86-282e-5662-8cd7-42b9fb93d405" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-9 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326053} {:answer/id #uuid "ee0d9ad7-a396-5711-bf79-bcf07da297d2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326068} {:answer/id #uuid "f967f9c1-953a-54c8-a8ce-01011a989f00" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326166}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324200} :answer-field/id #uuid "1200dc9e-5093-525d-82aa-0d957f5fb83d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326254}] :question/id #uuid "72ebe648-c9aa-5496-8f25-29cd029ad4fa" :question/math-academy-id "q-41775" :question/problem "Find the least-squares solution to the system of linear equations given below. You're given that the columns of the corresponding coefficient matrix are linearly independent.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{x}_{3} &=18 \\\\ {x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}-{x}_{3} &=18 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\hat{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\,\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -3 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}18 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 18 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 18 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}36 \\\\ 72 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}\\begin{bmatrix}9 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 18\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}36 \\\\ 72 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186134364 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9fc4c888-0edc-5f47-9684-d510b178bffb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132224} {:answer/id #uuid "c72e6176-4aa3-549f-ae33-06be5abb3961" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132225} {:answer/id #uuid "d3083521-1bf0-5b15-bbda-133ad3d59bdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ \\frac{2}{7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132226} {:answer/id #uuid "ec4088a5-1fa0-5fdf-bd0d-59411eff15d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132227} {:answer/id #uuid "6659e56b-a18d-5ce4-973e-68383d2f2164" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132228}] :answer-field/id #uuid "6f0ddf23-aa8e-58d8-8a18-760bf2952dba" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186132223} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "aab1554b-fae0-5335-a6a7-77698df741dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382112} {:answer/id #uuid "2009b66f-003d-5c80-8e48-abab88cb1420" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382113} {:answer/id #uuid "1487b100-1c31-5209-b048-3058cc674fa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ \\frac{2}{7}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382114} {:answer/id #uuid "433d99e6-601f-5df8-b751-d495ed88d741" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{1}{5} \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382115} {:answer/id #uuid "449cd155-31c2-5512-84f6-8af243475ed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382116}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382112} :answer-field/id #uuid "141813b9-42f5-5cea-9859-9368a52e5ca4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382111}] :question/id #uuid "2525e60a-78e9-5925-88e7-cb75c790f3bc" :question/math-academy-id "q-41777" :question/problem "Find the least-squares solution to the system of linear equations given below. You're given that the columns of the corresponding coefficient matrix are linearly independent.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=5 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2} &=2 \\\\ -3{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}x \\\\ y\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\hat{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -3 & -2\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}14 & 7 \\\\ 7 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{35}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -7 \\\\ -7 & 14\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326908 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "125e5ea0-2d09-53c7-bf5a-6db86f01788b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{11}{20} \\\\ -\\frac{7}{20}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324136} {:answer/id #uuid "16df845b-8aca-58e3-ae92-9d86f331bce3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{13}{20} \\\\ \\frac{1}{20}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324173} {:answer/id #uuid "24d2ae87-e1f9-50af-9aa6-98e8929a2d33" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{17}{20} \\\\ \\frac{3}{20}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324274} {:answer/id #uuid "b8e4ad4a-f6d5-57ac-9b52-100c6666021e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{20} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{20}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325558} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6ec109-3e58-5c22-b7fa-223132d14aab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{20} \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{20} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{20}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325558} :answer-field/id #uuid "24dd5431-2243-5962-ae01-cbb9b9be0bfc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326282}] :question/id #uuid "082f22b9-7dbc-5c7c-88d0-775a3d957e87" :question/math-academy-id "q-41776" :question/problem "Find the least-squares solution to the system of linear equations given below. You're given that the columns of the corresponding coefficient matrix are linearly independent.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}+{x}_{2} &=1 \\\\ 2{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} &=-1 \\\\ -{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2} &=0\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}}}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\hat{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 14\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{40}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{20} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{20}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186326909 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "383e5550-6206-5528-ade3-394d4573fe0b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-3 \\\\ \\frac{11}{25}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186324428} {:answer/id #uuid "b227f854-9e16-5626-bce0-ada038d08da2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325494} {:answer/id #uuid "b3a49e9d-022f-5b7d-94c6-abbb47e7bec8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{25} \\\\ \\frac{1}{75}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325514} {:answer/id #uuid "c031b973-4665-5e46-9b49-3b095d1d501d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{5} \\\\ \\frac{19}{25}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325625} {:answer/id #uuid "de40eb95-e222-557c-aadb-9cdef97d6b8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325910}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186325494} :answer-field/id #uuid "4e1a0373-21c1-5089-8385-c28dcb149d26" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186326346}] :question/id #uuid "b2442a57-a3cd-5f70-ab1c-b200915b57c3" :question/math-academy-id "q-41780" :question/problem "Find the least-squares solution to the system of linear equations given below. You're given that the columns of the corresponding coefficient matrix are linearly independent.\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2} &=-7 \\\\ -{x}_{1}-2{x}_{2} &=-4 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-4{x}_{2} &=12\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}}=\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix}}}.\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\hat{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -2 \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ -3 & -2 & -4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-7 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}14 & -16 \\\\ -16 & 29\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}26 \\\\ -19\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{150}\\begin{bmatrix}29 & 16 \\\\ 16 & 14\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}26 \\\\ -19\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366139 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f89186f2-808a-5375-8e88-e550363fce40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\frac{3}{5} \\\\ \\