t, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & -1 & -1 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-6 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\hat{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\hat{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\hat{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\hat{x}-b & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\hat{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186365066 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49a7bd03-adf3-5a48-adb8-d76ed491a021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365068} {:answer/id #uuid "85fe827a-334d-563d-b3ec-f6aa090b4374" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365069} {:answer/id #uuid "e16238df-b586-5a3a-b10f-36fe66a14e8c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365070} {:answer/id #uuid "5a641c91-fc27-54cb-8452-020ac9399775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365071} {:answer/id #uuid "76531132-2206-5f04-81b7-c44855988b0f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365072}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{21}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365068} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd7d2fbd-4032-5e0e-9ec2-d6247e90383e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186365067}] :question/id #uuid "653b302d-1e3a-540d-aafd-23e5eba2e8bd" :question/math-academy-id "q-140952" :question/problem "Consider the system $Ax=b$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\hat{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 & -1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 9\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{15}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\hat{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\hat{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\hat{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\hat{x}-b & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}-5 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\hat{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}=\\sqrt{21}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186366497 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "84388de8-73a2-569b-ab0e-277620cde274" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366499} {:answer/id #uuid "382fb806-1978-579d-89ed-efd0a6e81ee1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366500} {:answer/id #uuid "0472a83d-65e5-5013-b866-8c431be4a9a2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366501} {:answer/id #uuid "34dc0ee8-1ffc-5642-9583-1a5c8c9e0ce6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366502} {:answer/id #uuid "11152628-3c35-5a9f-9807-8452a3f695de" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366503}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366503} :answer-field/id #uuid "43418a64-7ce6-5fff-bf83-32f55a513389" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186366498}] :question/id #uuid "e6023681-5e35-5922-859f-00465fe3c2bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-85281" :question/problem "Consider the system $Ax=b$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\hat{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{5}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}5 \\\\ 5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\hat{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\hat{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\hat{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\hat{x}-b & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\hat{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-1)^{2}}=3\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382566 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6e98d845-002f-583e-8e2e-c38bbe7de8f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382568} {:answer/id #uuid "7786ed39-2dbb-5f7d-bf08-6bec28171c31" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382569} {:answer/id #uuid "cb964b5b-bac3-57a5-8203-f9e1ae78d687" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382570} {:answer/id #uuid "c739a3f6-5a92-5370-933d-3523a77208ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382571} {:answer/id #uuid "47cab409-32b1-5e78-9160-cf977247036e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382572}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{26}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382571} :answer-field/id #uuid "239e5903-65ea-585b-898e-25c3e72e9d67" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382567}] :question/id #uuid "81030c04-8049-5124-9acd-0f1fecb2eec0" :question/math-academy-id "q-85910" :question/problem "Consider the system $Ax=b$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are shown below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\hat{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\,\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 & -1 & 0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 & 0 & 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\hat{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\hat{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\hat{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\hat{x}-b & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}8 \\\\ 8\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 12 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -8 \\\\ -4 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\hat{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-8)^{2}+(-4)^{2}+(-2)^{2}}=2\\sqrt{26}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186382573 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db34a3a7-82db-516e-9b5f-f74695de47f9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382575} {:answer/id #uuid "231e106c-0303-5b69-9237-341c2dc82244" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382576} {:answer/id #uuid "b1264692-a197-5024-84dd-8409773b4cef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382577} {:answer/id #uuid "63c436ce-c5cd-5684-9714-4a097df7fdbc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382578} {:answer/id #uuid "4dce82c7-9228-540c-b08c-9cc8383746e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{17}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382579}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{19}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382575} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f3514e1-3487-5717-8374-c6a14d4839ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186382574}] :question/id #uuid "7ed86ff9-5c1b-5f36-88cb-573447ebe9b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-85919" :question/problem "Consider the system $Ax=b$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are shown below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\hat{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\,\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & -1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & -2 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 10\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{36}\\begin{bmatrix}10 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\hat{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\hat{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\hat{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\hat{x}-b & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}4 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 13 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 6\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -9 \\\\ -1 \\\\ -8\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\hat{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+(-5)^{2}+(-9)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(-8)^{2}}=3\\sqrt{19}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186482586 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "164af3d4-d329-5a63-9544-443eea1cc4f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481836} {:answer/id #uuid "2bbf719c-8336-5b63-8170-1187e7f4e55b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481885} {:answer/id #uuid "2daf4fd5-f4c3-5cde-bed6-b74154aa47b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481891} {:answer/id #uuid "8eaa36ae-b43e-5ed4-8193-ae54fff3942f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482110} {:answer/id #uuid "e5ce1773-5c8b-5827-b29e-4b8dba8f0126" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{35}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186481836} :answer-field/id #uuid "791b26ae-4f7f-58a8-b298-28b8f970263b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186482441}] :question/id #uuid "bbdebe64-e032-577f-8298-161c9dc3fe78" :question/math-academy-id "q-85285" :question/problem "Consider the system $Ax=b$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are shown below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\hat{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -1 & 0 & 1 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 4\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}16 \\\\ 16\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\hat{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\hat{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\hat{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\hat{x}-b & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 4\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}6 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 9 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -3 \\\\ -4\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\hat{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{3}^{2}+(-3)^{2}+(-4)^{2}}=\\sqrt{35}.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500322 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13c9ab58-bd09-5df1-8d1d-2d4ce831e5f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499698} {:answer/id #uuid "4fda416c-29ab-5041-9567-21fe9188edc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499807} {:answer/id #uuid "6123a26d-2828-5a47-a292-99e6c3705513" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499845} {:answer/id #uuid "bcbbd696-cd17-5e43-a03c-c815bdcc9a15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500039} {:answer/id #uuid "c898ab35-05fd-5fa1-8c7c-3ba6a9711cb3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500064}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499845} :answer-field/id #uuid "112e9326-3d57-5ecf-afb8-b6f921f35c4c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500187}] :question/id #uuid "7b37b44d-e7cb-5e9e-b8af-e9f1e4941b43" :question/math-academy-id "q-140953" :question/problem "Consider the system $Ax=b$, where the matrix $A$ and the vector $b$ are shown below. Given that the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, find the minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖.$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,b=\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First of all, we write the given system in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}}}\\overset{x}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}}} & =\\overset{b}{\\overset{⏞}{\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}}} \\\\ Ax & =b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can find the least-squares solution $\\hat{x}$ of the equation above by solving the corresponding normal equation, which we obtain by left-multiplying our original equation by ${A}^{T}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{T}\\,A\\hat{x} & ={A}^{T}b\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the columns of $A$ are linearly independent, the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A$ is invertible. Therefore, multiplying by $({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}$ on the left, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\hat{x} & =({A}^{T}\\,A)^{-1}{A}^{T}b \\\\  & ={(\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix})}^{-1}\\,\\,\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -1 & 2 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}}^{-1}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{45}\\begin{bmatrix}7 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}12 \\\\ -3\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe minimum value of $‖Ax-b‖$ is attained when $x=\\hat{x},$ which is the least-squares solution of the system $Ax=b.$ In this case, $A\\hat{x}$ represents the orthogonal projection of $b$ onto the column space of $A,$ and $‖A\\hat{x}-b‖$ is the distance between the vector $b$ and the column space. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A\\hat{x}-b & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ 0 \\\\ -1 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 3\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, \n\n$$\n‖A\\hat{x}-b‖=\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+{0}^{2}+{0}^{2}}=\\sqrt{3}.\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Distance Between a Vector to a Subspace of Solutions of a Linear System"}] :topic/math-academy-id 2166 :topic/title "The Least-Squares Solution of a Linear System (Without Collinearity)"}]}
